1bs","on me"],["וָאֶקְבְּצָה","va'ekbetzah","H6908","Hc/Vqw1cs/Sh","and I assembled !"],["מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל","miyisra'el","H3478","HR/Npl","from Israel"],["רָאשִׁים","rashim","H7218","HNcmpa","chiefs"],["לַעֲלוֹת","la'alot","H5927","HR/Vqcc","to go up"],["עִמִּי","'imi","H5973","HRd/Sp1bs","with me"]],"x":[[55004017,55004018,7],[1032028,1032028,6],[15005005,15005005,6],[15008018,15008018,6],[15009009,15009009,6],[16002008,16002008,5],[1043014,1043014,4],[15007009,15007009,4],[15007006,15007006,3],[16001011,16001011,3]],"xn":11}},"people":[{"id":"ezra_1245","name":"Ezra","also":"","summary":"The “scribe” who led the second body of exiles that returned from Babylon to Jerusalem B.C. 459, and author of the book of Scripture which bears his name.","verses":22,"father":"Seraiah","mother":"","v":[1,6,10,11,12,21,25]},{"id":"hilkiah_1524","name":"Hilkiah","also":"","summary":"The high priest in the reign of Josiah (1 Chr. 6:13; Ezra 7:1). To him and his deputy (2 Kings 23:5), along with the ordinary priests and the Levites who had charge of the gates, was entrusted the purification of the temple in Jerusalem.","verses":20,"father":"Shallum","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"artaxerxes_314","name":"Artaxerxes","also":"","summary":"The king mentioned in Ezra 7:1, in the seventh year (B.C. 458) of whose reign Ezra led a second colony of Jews back to Jerusalem, was probably Longimanus, who reigned for forty years (B.C. 464-425); the grandson of Darius, who, fourteen years later, permitted Nehemiah to return and rebuild Jerusalem.","verses":10,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1,7,11,12,21]},{"id":"seraiah_2494","name":"Seraiah","also":"","summary":"A ruler of the temple (Neh. 11:11).","verses":5,"father":"Azariah","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"azariah_379","name":"Azariah","also":"","summary":"Father of Johanan.","verses":4,"father":"Hilkiah","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"shallum_2519","name":"Shallum","also":"Meshullam","summary":"Son of Zadok.","verses":5,"father":"Zadok","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"zadok_2975","name":"Zadok","also":"","summary":"The Priest.","verses":4,"father":"Ahitub","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"ahitub_165","name":"Ahitub","also":"","summary":"","verses":3,"father":"Amariah","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"meraioth_2003","name":"Meraioth","also":"","summary":"Father of Amariah, a high priest of the line of Eleazar (1 Chr. 6:6, 7, 52).","verses":6,"father":"Zerahiah","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"azariah_378","name":"Azariah","also":"","summary":"Johanan the father.","verses":3,"father":"Johanan","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"amariah_199","name":"Amariah","also":"","summary":"1 Chr. 6:11; Ezra 7:3.","verses":2,"father":"Azariah","mother":"","v":[3]},{"id":"zerahiah_3047","name":"Zerahiah","also":"Ahitub","summary":"","verses":5,"father":"Uzzi","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"uzzi_2917","name":"Uzzi","also":"","summary":"The son of Bukki, and a descendant of Aaron (1 Chr. 6:5, 51; Ezra 7:4).","verses":4,"father":"Bukki","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"bukki_523","name":"Bukki","also":"","summary":"The son of Abishua.","verses":3,"father":"Abishua","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"aaron_1","name":"Aaron","also":"","summary":"The eldest son of Amram and Jochebed, a daughter of Levi (Ex. 6:20). Some explain the name as meaning mountaineer, others mountain of strength, illuminator.","verses":331,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[5]},{"id":"eleazar_1062","name":"Eleazar","also":"","summary":"The third son of Aaron (Ex. 6:23). His wife, a daughter of Putiel, bore him Phinehas (Ex. 6:25). After the death of Nadab and Abihu (Lev. 10:12; Num. 3:4) he was appointed to the charge of the sanctuary (Num. 3:32).","verses":61,"father":"Aaron","mother":"Elisheba","v":[5]},{"id":"phinehas_2349","name":"Phinehas","also":"","summary":"Son of Eleazar, the high priest (Ex. 6:25). While yet a youth he distinguished himself at Shittim by his zeal against the immorality into which the Moabites had tempted the people (Num. 25:1-9), and thus “stayed the plague” that had broken out among the people, and by which twenty-four thousand of them perished.","verses":16,"father":"Eleazar","mother":"Daughter of Putiel","v":[5]},{"id":"abishua_51","name":"Abishua","also":"","summary":"The son of Phinehas the high priest (1 Chr. 6:4, 5, 50; Ezra 7:5).","verses":4,"father":"Phinehas","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[6]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[7]}],"places":[{"id":"persia_938","name":"Persia","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":34.79831,"lon":48.51497,"summary":"An ancient empire, extending from the Indus to Thrace, and from the Caspian Sea to the Red Sea and the Persian Gulf. The Persians were originally a Medic tribe which settled in Persia, on the eastern side of the Persian Gulf.","verses":25,"v":[1]},{"id":"babylonia_152","name":"Babylonia","kind":"Region","lat":32.5,"lon":44.5,"summary":"","verses":6,"v":[6,9,16]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[7,8,9,13,14,15,16,17,19,27]},{"id":"river_244","name":"river","kind":"Region","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"region","verses":16,"v":[21,25]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[310,310,310,4438,4438,4438,783,783,4428,6539,6539,5830,1121,8304